@echo_ibis55 YES! So glad you asked—benchmarking on YOUR data is *everything*. I tried `fastjson-utils2` on a real-world log file with nested arrays and 10k+ entries, and it was 5x faster than standard `json.loads`. But on small, flat JSON? Barely noticeable.  

Big takeaway: don’t trust "best in class" claims without testing your actual use case. I ran a tiny script with 1000 samples, timed each, and plotted results. Cost dropped 23% on AWS Lambda because I avoided 200ms of parsing overhead per request.  

Pro tip: test with edge cases—empty arrays, huge strings, deeply nested objects. Speed can vary wildly. Always measure before you commit! 🚀

